    pr_ref:  # 269e
    description: "RESIDUAL of WI-finij, surfaced by draining its 11 (PR #1009, dev dc57e8cc33).\n\nTHE MEASURED GAP. Eleven pass-runs scanned files and emitted nothing. Six of\nthem had genuinely found no construct and now say so (`no_candidate_construct`,\n0 -> 6). The other FIVE found their construct and emitted nothing anyway:\n\n  annotation-convention   routes/dispatches found, no target symbol to bind\n  di-resolution           bindings found, resolve to no symbol\n  ipc                     patterns found, `continue` before the symbol append\n  wasm-bindgen            wasm imports found, matching export absent\n  message-dispatch        writes found without reads, or reads without writes\n\nIn every one the construct IS PRESENT in the repository. What failed is the\nRELATION: an import with no export, a binding with no symbol, a write with no\nread. The axis has no value for that state, so they land in `unreported`,\nwhich means CANNOT DETERMINE.\n\nWHY THIS IS WORTH A ROW. Before the drain this population was invisible --\nundifferentiated inside a bucket that also held \"genuinely found nothing\". It\nis now isolated and countable at five on the self-survey, and it is the\npopulation a consumer most needs distinguished: \"your repo has no GraphQL\nresolvers\" and \"your repo has GraphQL resolvers we could not connect to a\nschema\" are opposite answers to \"is this linker useful here?\".\n\nWHAT IS NOT BEING ASSERTED. That a new value SHOULD be declared. Adding one is\nADR-0024 scaffolding plus an axis-conformance decision, and a value with no\nproducer is exactly the trap INV-hujog is stuck in (`prerequisite_absent`,\ndeclared, zero producers, and a deferral whose re-open trigger therefore cannot\nfire). The difference here, and the reason this is a better candidate than that\none: THE PRODUCERS ALREADY EXIST. The five call sites above are written, live\nand measured, so a value declared for them would be wired on arrival rather\nthan aspirational.\n\nDECISION REQUIRED FROM THE OWNER, not pre-judged:\n  (a) declare a seventh value (name unproposed here) and wire those five; or\n  (b) rule that `unreported` is the correct home for an unpaired construct and\n      say so IN THE AXIS DOCSTRING, so the next reader does not re-open this.\n\nEither way the honest state is recorded. What must NOT happen is stamping the\nfive `no_candidate_construct`: that is the WI-finij defect -- a positive claim\ninferred from an absence -- committed a second time inside the axis built to\ncure it.\n\nEVIDENCE: self-survey at dev dc57e8cc33, 97 analysis_runs,\n{'': 43, no_candidate_files: 43, no_candidate_construct: 6, unreported: 5}.\nRe-derivable: hypergumbo survey . --out F, then group analysis_runs by\nsilence_reason."  # 269e
    fields: {}  # 269e
