- op: discuss  # 57de
  at: '2026-09-17T00:07:51Z'  # 57de
  by: agent  # 57de
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 57de
  clock: 4  # 57de
  nonce: 57de  # 57de
  message: "DONE (PR #1010, dev e83f2b997f, ADR-0054). Closed on BEHAVIOURAL evidence: a\nlive self-survey, not a proxy.\n\nWHAT WAS DECIDED. A distinguished-expert review ruled DECLARE, against the\nruling I had shipped hours earlier, and its three stated grounds were each\nrefuted by the tree: the value would be \"a seventh member\" (the vocabulary\nalready held seven), with \"a single producer\" (eleven call sites through one\nhelper -- the same shape as no_candidate_construct, which is considered good\ndesign) and \"no consumer\" (summarize_silence and format_silence_summary count\nand print by whatever name they find, wired at cli.py). That last one is the\nwhole difference from prerequisite_absent and I had it backwards.\n\nThe decisive argument is one I had not made: `unreported` is declared to mean\nthe pass \"produced nothing AND DID NOT SAY WHY\", but these five bodies COMPUTE\nthe fact and discard it -- the helper returned \"\" on the branch holding the\nanswer. Not abstention; a disclosure the producer holds and declines to make.\n\nEVIDENCE, before -> after on the hypergumbo self-survey, 97 analysis_runs:\n    before:  no_candidate_files=43  no_candidate_construct=6  unreported=5\n    after:   no_candidate_files=43  no_candidate_construct=7\n             candidates_unresolved=4  unreported=0\n  candidates_unresolved: annotation-convention, di-resolution, ipc,\n  message-dispatch. Re-derivable: hypergumbo survey . --out F, group\n  analysis_runs by silence_reason. NOTE /tmp is tmpfs here -- a ~250 MB survey\n  written there will OOM the box; use real disk.\n\nTHE EXPERT'S OWN PREDICTION WAS WRONG, AND MEASURING IS WHAT CAUGHT IT. It\npredicted the one-line producer change would take unreported to 0. It took it\nto 2. FOUR return paths never call the helper at all, which the verdict filed\nas a LATENT residual that \"will appear on a JS/TS or Solidity corpus\" -- while\ntwo of them were firing on this corpus as it wrote that. wasm-bindgen returns\nearly when no Rust exports exist and its WRAPPER then scans 14 files, so the\nrun reported files with the body never having spoken; message-dispatch passed\nits bail with both sides non-empty and matched no pairs. Closed as a CLASS\n(all four), not as the two that happened to fire. There is consequently NO\nresidual row to file -- nothing is left uncovered.\n\nTHE NAME describes the PASS, not the repository, and that was a change of mind\non reading the code: ipc rejects some candidates on a quality filter with no\npairing attempted (`if not channel: continue`), so \"missing counterpart\" would\nbe false for it. A pass also cannot distinguish an absent counterpart (correct\nno-op) from its own matcher missing one (recall defect) -- the axis says those\nneed opposite responses.\n\nFILING, corrected by the test suite: first written as docs/audits/0019 and\nREJECTED by test_audit_findings. audit_findings._REGISTRIES binds exactly three\nregistry-backed axes (Edge.edge_type, Symbol.kind, Edge.evidence_type) and\nVALID_VERDICTS is a closed frozenset; AnalysisRun.silence_reason is a\nLIGHTWEIGHT catalog-derived axis and cannot be named in a kind: audit_verdicts\nblock at all. Filed as ADR-0054. docs/surveys/python-stdlib-module-io-\nenumeration.md hit the same validator on its own first attempt at the same\nnumber -- the trap has now caught two sessions, so ADR-0054 records the rule\nexplicitly: docs/audits/ is for the three registry-backed axes.\n\nSTATED HONESTLY, and carried into ir.py: unreported=0 MEASURES THE CORPUS, NOT\nCOMPLETION. 53 of 64 linker modules make no body claim at all and would land\nthere on a corpus where they are active. The \"the unreported count is the size\nof the remaining work\" gloss is removed from the field comment.\n\nRE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS (ADR-0054), both fireable off ordinary bakeoff output:\nT1 candidates_unresolved reaches >=60% of silent pass-runs (absorbing, not\ndifferentiating); T2 a run stamped candidates_unresolved is traced to a pass\nwhose counterpart IS present in the same behavior map (a recall defect wearing\na correct-no-op label)."  # 57de
